-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  float_arith.adam - Float arithmetic (M3.6b). float64 + - * / of variables
  (0.1 + 0.2 is 0.30000000000000004), a divide by +0.0 giving +inf / -inf,
  0 / 0 and inf - inf the default NaN, a NaN's payload carried through + and
  * from either side, unary minus as the sign bit flipped (-0.0 from +0.0,
  +0.0 from -0.0, a NaN keeps its payload), +0.0 * -1.0 is -0.0, unary plus,
  a nested expression, arithmetic on parameters; the compounds += -= *= /=
  on a local, a record field, through a pointer and on a module variable;
  float32 + - * / rounded to float32 (0.1f + 0.2f), an overflow to +inf,
  16777216.0f + 1.0f staying 16777216.0f (round to even), -0.0f, the
  float32 compounds and a float32 NaN's payload through - and +. Each float
  is shown by its IEEE bits read back through an overlay (float64 as int64,
  float32 as uint32), through ucrtbase (_i64toa + puts). Expected lines:
  scripts\adam\float_arith_expect.py.
*******************************************************************************/

